From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:48:09 -0700
Subject: Fix uninitialized pixel reads in ConvertVideoFrameToRGBPixels()

1. Handle RGB frames whose stride or plane data pointer is not aligned
   to bytesPerPixel() in ConvertVideoFrameToRGBPixelsTask() by copying
   each row into an aligned row buffer before calling
   SkPixmap::readPixels(), and CHECK() that SkPixmap::readPixels()
   succeeds. Also spanify PlaneMetaData::data using base::raw_span.

2. Allocate the visible rect size instead of coded_size in
   DownShiftHighbitVideoFrame(), and clear dst_pixmap to transparent
   black in ConvertVideoFrameToRGBPixels() if
   DownShiftHighbitVideoFrame() returns nullptr.

Fixed: 574311093, 574897062
Change-Id: Ic7de977ce7a8e332fca456e38473f802c8c22964
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8613831
Reviewed-by: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1723041}

